    level: 'orta', cefr: 'B2', konu: ['akış'],
    q: 'In 1799, a large slab of dark stone covered in writing was found in Egypt. ----. Because the Greek part could be read, scholars realised that the stone offered a key to the other two scripts. Even so, progress was slow, and it was not until 1822 that Jean-François Champollion announced that he had worked out how hieroglyphs functioned.',
